<title>INDIA: India's HPCL said seeking tie-up with Exxon.</title>
<headline>India's HPCL said seeking tie-up with Exxon.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-09-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>India's Hindustan Petroleum Corporation Ltd (HPCL) is seeking an equity tie-up with Exxon Corp of the U.S. for a new refinery HPCL plans to build on the west coast, oil industry sources said.</p>
<p>The sources said HPCL is looking for a new partner to replace Oman Oil Company, which has not taken up its 26 percent equity entitlement in the project, the sources said.</p>
<p>HPCL and the Oman Oil Company last year signed a memorandum of understanding to float a joint venture.</p>
<p>&quot;A HPCL team is talking to Exxon,&quot; said a source, who declined to be named.</p>
<p>HPCL officials were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom +91-22-265 9000</p>
